{
 "_doc": "AKS-74U gunfire: five separately delivered layers, all timelined from the shot instant (t = 0) so the engine starts them together. See build_fire.py. src paths relative to the extracted Tactical Shooter Pack. 5.45 carbine: short barrel = bright crack + flash, so the close chain leans on 3-4 kHz and the body is kept tight. Round 4: fire_sub is built from real recordings only (low-passed shot + the same shot pitched down); no synthesis. Round 4: no algorithmic reverb anywhere; the far layer is the real recorded tail, low-passed and compressed. Round 5 (2026-10-03 revamp): 8 close variants, every one layered with a TR15 shot twice over - its crack (high-passed) and its body (150 Hz - 6 kHz, 8 dB down) - over three AK105 recordings with Mk14 weight on some; the chain's compressor and saturation eased so the shot keeps its crest. The far layer is real AK shots recorded 50 m away in a valley (Pole Position), a different shot per variant.",
